# Paths that legitimately contain secret-SHAPED content and no secret.
#
# Read by the branch-safety scan (workaholic:release-scan) as :(exclude) globs.
# This is a pre-declaration made in review, not an override: the file is
# committed, so every entry lands in a diff a human reads, and secret findings
# stay non-overridable everywhere else.
#
# Keep every entry as narrow as the file it excuses, and only after trying to
# fix the finding at its source. A directory glob here would silently cover the
# next file added beside it, and a PRODUCTION file listed here means a real key
# hardcoded in it later goes unreported.

# The GCP OAuth spec. It exercises the RFC 7523 token exchange, so it must
# contain the response vocabulary -- `access_token`, `token_type`, `Bearer` --
# with values beside it, which is a credential shape by construction. The
# values are stubs (`stub-access-token`); the RSA key pair the spec signs with
# is GENERATED FRESH at run time by `node:crypto` and is deliberately not
# committed, so this file holds no key material at all.
#
# Two sibling findings in this branch were NOT declared here, because they were
# fixable at the source: a doc comment in the production `vendors/webcrypto.ts`
# spelled out the PEM armour line verbatim, and the stub token used `ya29.`,
# Google's real access-token prefix. Both were reworded instead.
